--- Mid-outage observations while ruby was powered off (~15:54:05Z - 16:02Z UTC) ---
* runner-1 aat-ruby.service exited 0/SUCCESS (ACPI S5 Power down) at 22:54:05 WIB / 15:54:05 UTC; with Restart=on-failure, QEMU did not auto-reboot on clean guest poweroff.
* ruby node entered NotReady; CoreDNS was scheduled solely on ruby, stalling cluster DNS until CoreDNS evicted & rescheduled onto aqua.
* Single-replica redpanda-0 (pinned to ruby in k8s/base/broker.yaml) went unreachable; aggregator /health BrokerPinger returned HTTP 503 so surviving aggregator pods (aqua, akane) went 0/1 Ready.
* Mid-outage API probes: GET https://audit-aat.darsu.dev/internal/audit/checksum -> HTTP 503 ("no available server"); GET https://aat.darsu.dev/api/v1/hazards?limit=5 -> HTTP 500 (5000ms upstream timeout to aggregator:8083).
* Note: surviving aggregator pods also logged "all storage units are unavailable: begin lease tx: context deadline exceeded" while store-ruby (10.42.3.x) packets dropped on powered-off ruby.

